nCancel (u² + 144) (nonzero):\n\n1/(2(144 - 5u)) = 225/(169 · 18(u + 16))\n\n169 · 18(u + 16) = 225 · 2(144 - 5u)\n169 · 18(u + 16) = 450(144 - 5u)\n\n169 · 18 = 3042. 450 · 144 = 64800.\n\n3042(u + 16) = 64800 - 2250u\n3042u + 48672 = 64800 - 2250u\n3042u + 2250u = 64800 - 48672\n5292u = 16128\nu = 16128/5292\n\nLet me simplify. GCD? 16128 and 5292.\n5292 = 4·1323 = 4·3·441 = 4·3·21² = 4·3·441. Actually 5292 = 5292. 5292/4 = 1323. 1323/3 = 441 = 21². So 5292 = 4·3·441 = 12·441 = 12·21² = 5292. Hmm, 12·441 = 5292. Yes.\n\n16128: 16128/4 = 4032. 4032/4 = 1008. 1008/4 = 252. 252/4 = 63. So 16128 = 256·63 = 256·9·7 = 2304·7. So 16128 = 2^8 · 3^2 · 7.\n\n5292 = 4·1323 = 4·3·441 = 4·3·9·49 = 4·27·49 = 2^2 · 3^3 · 7^2.\n\nGCD = 2^2 · 3^2 · 7 = 4·9·7 = 252.\n\n16128/252 = 64. 5292/252 = 21.\n\nu = 64/21.\n\nSo a = u + 5 = 64/21 + 5 = 64/21 + 105/21 = 169/21.\n\nCheck: a = 169/21 ≈ 8.05, which is in [0, 14]. Good.\n\nNow compute t and s.\n\nt = (u² + 144)/(18(u + 16))\n\nu = 64/21. u² = 4096/441.\nu² + 144 = 4096/441 + 144 = 4096/441 + 63504/441 = 67600/441.\n\nu + 16 = 64/21 + 16 = 64/21 + 336/21 = 400/21.\n\n18(u + 16) = 18·400/21 = 7200/21 = 2400/7.\n\nt = (67600/441)/(2400/7) = (67600/441)·(7/2400) = 67600·7/(441·2400) = 473200/(1058400).\n\nSimplify: 473200/1058400. Divide by 100: 4732/10584. Divide by 4: 1183/2646. \n\nHmm let me recompute. 67600·7 = 473200. 441·2400 = 1058400. \n\n473200/1058400. GCD? Let's divide both by 200: 2366/5292. Divide by 2: 1183/2646. \n\n1183 = 1183. Is 1183 prime? 1183/7 = 169. Yes! 1183 = 7·169 = 7·13². 2646 = 2·1323 = 2·3·441 = 2·3·9·49 = 2·27·49 = 2·3³·7². \n\nGCD of 1183 and 2646: 1183 = 7·169, 2646 = 2·3³·7² = 2·27·49. GCD = 7. 1183/7 = 169, 2646/7 = 378.\n\nt = 169/378. \n\nCheck: 169 = 13². 378 = 2·189 = 2·27·7 = 2·3³·7. GCD(169, 378) = 1. Good.\n\ns = (225/169)t = (225/169)·(169/378) = 225/378 = 75/126 = 25/42.\n\nNow compute D and E.\n\nD = (5 + 9t, 12 - 12t) = (5 + 9·169/378, 12 - 12·169/378).\n\n9·169/378 = 1521/378 = 169/42 (d